    "q-35347": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35347",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Given $G=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))$, we reduce $G$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{11}{4} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))=0.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
